      "side": 1,
      "message": "This fixes the missing update. I think the shift width is off though: 1 is int, so for a first_unused of 31 this evaluates to INT_MIN and sign-extends on the |\u003d into the u64, setting bits 31 through 63 in one go. used_device_id_mask then reads as U64_MAX, so the next add returns -EINVAL and, as in the earlier round, cwriter_write stops on that command and the driver hits its completion timeout. Above 31 the shift is undefined as well. BIT_ULL(first_unused) would keep it to the one bit, and would match track_device_id_remove just below, which already uses BIT().",
      "revId": "2e129312028a352947eed959588d2303a06aafa3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
