        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T12:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there may be a problem with which bytes end up in the queue. cmd is filled from cmd_le at line 410 and process_cmd validates that copy, but the memcpy here re-reads cmd_le, and cmd_host_base is the shadow queue the host driver writes into. A host CPU that rewrites the entry between the two reads has its command validated in one form and submitted in another, so the device-id tracking and ITT pinning that process_cmd performed need not describe what the GIC is actually programmed with. Could we fetch once into a local and use that for both, something like:\n\n```\n      struct its_cmd_block raw \u003d *cmd_le;\n\n      for (i \u003d 0; i \u003c ARRAY_SIZE(cmd.raw_cmd); i++)\n              cmd.raw_cmd[i] \u003d le64_to_cpu(raw.raw_cmd_le[i]);\n      ...\n      memcpy(its-\u003ecmd_hyp_base + its-\u003ecmd_offset, \u0026raw, sizeof(raw));\n```",
      "revId": "2e129312028a352947eed959588d2303a06aafa3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "72d9172e_4630e7ac",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/its_emulate.c",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 419,
