        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T12:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Relatedto the above, I think the flush is on the wrong address. cmd is the local snapshot, while the entry the GIC reads is the one just written at its-\u003ecmd_hyp_base + its-\u003ecmd_offset, so on the needs_flush path the queue entry itself is never cleaned to PoC. With the single fetch above it would want the destination, gic_flush_dcache_to_poc(its-\u003ecmd_hyp_base + its-\u003ecmd_offset, sizeof(raw)).",
      "revId": "2e129312028a352947eed959588d2303a06aafa3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12f5fee8_103ada28",
