        "id": 1782620
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-27T12:54:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "needs_flush is derived here once, but I don\u0027t think the CBASER shareability it reflects is fixed for the lifetime of the ITS. cbaser_write only replaces the size and address fields, so the shareability and cacheability bits stay host-writable, and ctlr_write only refuses the transition to enabled while not quiescent, so a host can disable the ITS, rewrite GITS_CBASER shareability, and enable it again. After that needs_flush no longer matches the live CBASER and the command queue is maintained under the wrong policy. Could we either recompute needs_flush in cbaser_write, or hold the shareability bits at the value snapshotted here, the same way the address is held?",
      "revId": "2e129312028a352947eed959588d2303a06aafa3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
